  vendor/die/db/PE/packer_NsPack.2.sg
  vendor/die/db/PE/packer_WinUpack.2.sg

vendor/die/fsg-patterns.json contains 44 derived FSG entry-point patterns.
vendor/die/entry-patterns.json contains 61 additional direct-entry branches:
ASPack 14, Petite 11, MEW 4, PECompact 8, RLPack 2 (EXE form only), tElock 5,
PELock 1, NsPack 6 and (Win)Upack 10. Relative-jump/string-pattern branches,
post-match version overrides and other fallbacks are not represented there.
src/core/detect.js translates selected FSG/UPX/MPRESS branches into bounded
JavaScript and labels separate section-name heuristics. These adaptations
are a documented subset, not the complete DIE engine or database.

4. RetDec-derived LZMAT decoding and MPRESS reconstruction

Source: https://github.com/avast/retdec
Fixed commit: 9450585772e6f1c18e5f0b2ad5518a18d6bce71e
License: MIT; complete original text: licenses/retdec-MIT.txt.
Copyright (c) 2017 Avast Software

src/core/codecs/lzmat.js is a bounded JavaScript adaptation of:
  src/unpacker/decompression/lzmat/lzmat_data.cpp
src/core/unpackers/mpress.js adapts MPRESS layout, CALL/JMP restoration and
PE reconstruction logic from:
  src/unpackertool/plugins/mpress/mpress.cpp

The project implements the selected PE32 LZMAT stub 0x29f / fix 0x35 path.
It does not incorporate the complete RetDec distribution or claim support
for all RetDec plugins, MPRESS variants or runtime behavior.

src/core/codecs/nrv.js adapts RetDec NRV2B/2D/2E LE32 decoders and bit readers.
src/core/unpackers/upx.js adapts PE header/import/relocation hint and unfilter
semantics from src/unpackertool/plugins/upx/ at the same fixed MIT revision.
PE acceptance is limited to the documented NRV2B short-stub/filter-0x26
analysis-only output. The GPL UPX/UCL/ClamAV implementations are not bundled.

